    {
      "filename": "Aliiolani Hale (2846900127).jpg",
      "title": "File:Aliiolani Hale (2846900127).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Aliiolani_Hale_%282846900127%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aliiolani_Hale_(2846900127).jpg",
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 853,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Cliff from Arlington, Virginia, USA",
      "description": "Although the building was designed to be a palace, Kamehameha V realized that the Hawaiian government desperately needed a government building. At that time, the several buildings in Honolulu used by the government were very small and cramped, clearly inadequate for the growing Hawaiian government. Thus, when Kamehameha V ordered construction of Ali’iōlani Hale, he commissioned it as a government office building instead of a palace.",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 1 December 2007, 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "ali-iolani-hale-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "87z9",
      "smallPath": "_m/8/7/z/9/ali-iolani-hale-wp/aliiolani-hale-2846900127-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Aliiolani Hale (2847734546).jpg",
      "title": "File:Aliiolani Hale (2847734546).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f2/Aliiolani_Hale_%282847734546%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aliiolani_Hale_(2847734546).jpg",
      "width": 853,
      "height": 1280,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Cliff from Arlington, Virginia, USA",
      "description": "In 1911, the building was extensively renovated to help solve these space problems. The entire interior of the building was gutted and rebuilt, giving the building's interior a completely new floor plan. Since the building was originally designed to be a palace, its floor plan was not adequate for its later usage as a judicial building. The new layout of the building fixed this problem. The size of the territorial government continued to grow. In the 1940s, a new wing was added to the building to help alleviate the growing problem of overcrowding. The architects who designed the new wing tried to blend it in with the original building that dated back to the 1870s. In 1972 Aliiolani Hale was added to the United States National Register of Historic Places.",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 1 December 2007, 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "ali-iolani-hale-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "87z9",
      "smallPath": "_m/8/7/z/9/ali-iolani-hale-wp/aliiolani-hale-2847734546-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Aliiolani Hale (2846900379).jpg",
      "title": "File:Aliiolani Hale (2846900379).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Aliiolani_Hale_%282846900379%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aliiolani_Hale_(2846900379).jpg",
      "width": 853,
      "height": 1280,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Cliff from Arlington, Virginia, USA",
      "description": "Kamehameha V laid the cornerstone for the building on February 19, 1872. He died before the building was completed, and it was dedicated in 1874 by one of his successors, King David Kalākaua. At the time, Hawaiian media criticized the building's extravagant design, suggesting that the building be converted into a palace as originally designed.",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 1 December 2007, 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "ali-iolani-hale-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "87z9",
      "smallPath": "_m/8/7/z/9/ali-iolani-hale-wp/aliiolani-hale-2846900379-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Aliiolani Hale (2847732892).jpg",
      "title": "File:Aliiolani Hale (2847732892).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Aliiolani_Hale_%282847732892%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aliiolani_Hale_(2847732892).jpg",
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 853,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Cliff from Arlington, Virginia, USA",
      "description": "Ali’iōlani Hale was originally designed in a Renaissance revival style by Australian Thomas Rowe as the royal palace for King Kamehameha V. In the Hawaiian language, Ali’iōlani Hale means \"House of the heavenly King\"; also, the name \"Ali’iōlani\" was one of the given names of Kamehameha V.",
      "dateCreated": "Taken on 1 December 2007, 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "ali-iolani-hale-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "87z9",
      "smallPath": "_m/8/7/z/9/ali-iolani-hale-wp/aliiolani-hale-2847732892-small.webp"
    }
